    "description": {
      "type": "String",
      "label": "Description",
      "value": "<p>The usually piebald Strigany Cob (Cob for short) has feathered heels and a long mane and tail. The traditional horse of travelling fairs, the Cob is famous for pulling caravans and Strigany&nbsp;vardos. It is often mistaken for a dray because of its heavy frame and obvious strength, but the horse is considerably more versatile. Known for its gentle nature and hard-working spirit, the breed is capable of almost any duty, which it usually fulfils with no complaint. Most Cobs rarely grow taller than 15 hands.</p>"
